{"speak":true,"message":"Astra: You did set a goal and produce a context summary. Those are visible actions; whether they improve efficiency remains untested. Let’s leave that broader question open for now.

Look at your context summary as a handoff for continuing this same work. If that were all you retained, would you know which unfinished decision to resume? Spend attention on the passage whose presence or absence most affects that, rather than adding more principles.

Compare that passage with the visible exchange. In your own concise wording, say what the comparison establishes, what remains uncertain, and what change you choose to make. Then make that change in the summary now. The immediate question is whether the revised text preserves information needed to continue; any claim about improved interaction efficiency can wait.","rationale":"Acknowledges completed textual actions, leaves efficiency unresolved, and shifts from repeated trial requests to a child-chosen, evidence-grounded handoff edit."}
